{title: 142 - Angels We Have Heard on High}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #142 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 142}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Angels we [Gm]have [F]heard on high Sweetly singing [Am]o'er [Dm]the [C7/E]plains,
[Am]And [Dm]the [F]mountains [Dm]in reply [C7]Echoing [Bb]their joy-ous [C/E]strains.
[F/A]Glo [C]ria [Bb]in [F/C]excelsis [Dm/F]Deo!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Gm]Gloria, [C7/E]in [F]excelsis [Dm]Deo!
[F/A]Gloria, in [Bb]excelsis [F]Deo!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Shepherds, why this [C7]jubilee?
[Am]Why [F]your [Dm]joyous [Gm]strains [C7/E]prolong?
[Am]What [C/E]the [F]gladsome [C7]tidings [Bb/D]be
[F/A]Which [C]inspire [F/C]your [C]heavenly [Dm/F]song?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Come to Bethlehem and [Dm]see
[Am]Christ [C/E]Whose [F]birth [Dm/F]the [C7]angels [Bb/D]sing;
[Am]Come, [C/E]adore [Dm/F]on [C7]bended [Bb/D]knee,
[F/A]Christ [C]the [Bb]Lord, [F/C]the newborn [Dm/F]King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]See Him in a [C7]manger [Dm]laid,
[Am]Whom [C/E]the [F]choirs [Dm/F]of [C7]angels [Bb/D]praise;
[Am]Mary, [F]Joseph, [C7]lend [F]your [Bb/D]aid,
[F/A]While our hearts [C]in [F]love [Dm]we raise.
{end_of_verse}
